# =============================================================================
# deploy/ - keep credentials and operator scratch out of git
#
# The root .gitignore already covers .env and .env.* by filename. This file adds
# the deployment-specific artefacts.
#
# Railway keeps its configuration in the dashboard (project variables, volumes,
# TCP proxies), so there is no checked-in state to ignore here - only things an
# operator is likely to leave lying around.
# =============================================================================

# --- Generated runtime secrets ----------------------------------------------
# A one-time credential printout, exported MQTT credentials, bcrypt hashes.
# Never commit these: they bypass the dashboard's variable store.
secrets/

# --- Local certificate material ---------------------------------------------
# Only relevant if you front the broker with your own TLS terminator, since
# Railway's TCP proxy is raw TCP and hands you no certificate to store.
*.pem
*.key

# --- Operator scratch --------------------------------------------------------
# Notes taken during a deployment that should not be published.
NOTES.local.md
